unibench's forkserver_libafl_reusing fuzzer, forkserver -> in-process, and
nothing else.

Applies after fuzzers/reusing_forkserver_cc/src/main.rs -- the fuzzer the
unibench reusing arm runs -- is copied over fuzzers/fuzzbench/src/lib.rs at
LibAFL_reusing 7c98c7fd (see builder.Dockerfile). 7c98c7fd is the unibench
arm's 4f590eb2 plus one reusing_core change an in-process fuzzer needs: each
try's cursor is saved before the try runs, so a restart after a crash resumes
past it instead of replaying it forever. Its other change, with_max_base(), is
unused here; ReusingEnergyStage::new() keeps unibench's cap of 128. The diff
to src/lib.rs is therefore the complete difference from that fuzzer:

  - executor   ForkserverExecutor -> InProcessExecutor over the target's
               LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput, after LLVMFuzzerInitialize
  - observer   the edges map in __AFL_SHM_ID shared memory -> the same map
               in this process (std_edges_map_observer, same name)
  - tokens     the tokens the forkserver target sends -> autotokens() from
               this binary
  - restarts   SimpleEventManager -> SimpleRestartingEventManager: a crash
               kills this process, so a fresh one resumes from the state left
               in shared memory. FromSeed marks the corpus only on a fresh
               start; after a restart the corpus holds finds too
  - output     the target's stdout/stderr go to /dev/null, as the forkserver
               child's did; the logger (the reusing stage's counters), the
               monitor and the fuzzer's own messages write to a copy of stdout
  - CLI        no target executable, target arguments, --debug-child or
               --signal; libafl_main() is the entry the target's main calls

Cargo.toml and src/bin/libafl_cc.rs take the unibench reusing crate's
instrumentation and dependencies: trace-pc-guard and AutoTokens only (no
trace-cmp, no CmpLogRtn pass), libafl with track_hit_feedbacks, clap with
derive, env_logger, log, reusing_core.

